Q: Call a function with the submit button in HTML A: <p>Here are 3 ways:</p>
<h3>Form <code>onsubmit</code> attribute</h3>
<p>In your form you can add the attribute <code>onsubmit</code>:</p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;form onsubmit=&quot;gtag_report_conversion('https://your-optional-callback-url.com')&quot;&gt;
  &lt;!-- ... --&gt;
&lt;/form&gt;
</code></pre>
<h3>Form <code>onsubmit</code> property</h3>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;form id=&quot;myForm&quot;&gt;
  &lt;!-- ... --&gt;
&lt;/form&gt;
</code></pre>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>document.querySelector('#myForm').onsubmit = (event) =&gt; {
  event.preventDefault(); // To prevent the page from reloading because of the form submission
  gtag_report_conversion('https://your-optional-callback-url.com');
  // ... Other stuff you want to do with the form submission
}
</code></pre>
<h3>Form <code>onsubmit</code> Event Listener</h3>
<p>Same HTML as above</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>document.querySelector('#myForm').addEventListener('submit', (event) =&gt; {
  event.preventDefault(); // To prevent the page from reloading because of the form submission
  gtag_report_conversion('https://your-optional-callback-url.com');
  // ... Other stuff you want to do with the form submission
});
</code></pre>
